1
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
¡Qué bonito amor! is a drama film directed by Mauricio de la Serna.

2
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Bride backs out of her wedding at the last possible minute; she and her fiance get
caught up in a power-struggle that ends with both running for mayor.

3
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Angélica María Hartman Ortiz (born September 27, 1944) is an
American-born Mexican singer and actress.

4
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Referred to as "La Novia de México" ("Mexico's Sweetheart"), she began her career as a child actress in films of the
Golden Age of Mexican cinema, such as Pecado (1951), Una mujer decente (1951), and Mi esposa y la otra (1952).

5
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
During the 1960s, she rose to prominence as a teen idol through her roles in films
and telenovelas, concurrently launching a successful music career.

6
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
Her recordings of compositions by Armando Manzanero established her as a popular singer of rock and roll and pop ballads, with hit songs
including the Billboard Hot Latin Tracks top 40-singles "El hombre de mi vida", "Reina y cenicienta", "Prohibido", and "El taconazo".

7
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
She has received numerous accolades for her contributions to music, film, and television, including a Latin Grammy Lifetime Achievement
Award, three Premios TVyNovelas, two Ariel Awards (including the Golden Ariel), and a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.
